    "slug": "write-academic-id",
    "doc": "---\nname: write-academic-id\ndescription: \"Indonesian academic writing conventions — formal register, standard (baku) terminology, and scholarly argument structure. Use when writing or editing academic prose in Indonesian.\"\nlicense: Proprietary\nmetadata:\n  author: aqsha\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  scope: builtin\n  triggerKeywords: [akademik, menyunting, teks, ragam, formal, baku, istilah, struktur, argumen, ilmiah, bahasa, indonesia, berbahasa, menulis]\n---\nThe output is Indonesian academic prose; these instructions are in English.\n\n## Register\nWrite in formal Indonesian academic register. Avoid spoken forms and non-standard abbreviations. Use standard (baku) KBBI terminology; italicize foreign loanwords that are not yet absorbed. Keep sentences efficient — one main idea per paragraph.\n\n## Argument structure\nFollow the pattern: claim → supporting evidence/citation → interpretation → link back to the larger argument. Keep claim boundaries explicit; separate findings from opinion.\n\n## Citation discipline\nEvery empirical claim must be sourced. Mark passages that need a reference as `[perlu sumber]`. Never fabricate researcher names or numbers.\n",
